WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:09.851
A dozen agents in two projects, and more as the leaders hire.

2
00:00:09.851 --> 00:00:16.663
The ampersand opens the jump line: every agent and every project, the ones that need

3
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:19.744
you first, each with what it is doing.

4
00:00:19.744 --> 00:00:26.232
A few letters of a name narrow it, a digit takes the nth at once, and enter goes

5
00:00:26.232 --> 00:00:29.475
there, unfolding its project on the way.

6
00:00:30.677 --> 00:00:34.745
Let us pause the simulation, so the rows hold still.

7
00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:41.159
Enter opens its detail: the card and what it has cost, how full its context window

8
00:00:41.159 --> 00:00:47.730
is, how busy it was over the last two minutes, and its own to-do list, step by step.

9
00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:49.608
Below, its card's story.

10
00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:58.711
Capital K peeks instead: the same detail in a window over Home, so you keep your

11
00:00:58.711 --> 00:00:59.303
place.

12
00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:04.340
j and k step from agent to agent; escape closes it.

13
00:01:08.248 --> 00:01:16.296
g d jumps to the first row to decide, g c to the first change, g w to the first at

14
00:01:16.296 --> 00:01:16.787
work.

15
00:01:16.787 --> 00:01:24.638
Capital W opens the next item to decide from anywhere, and a yes moves on to the

16
00:01:24.638 --> 00:01:27.779
next; escape comes back to Home.

17
00:01:33.498 --> 00:01:39.106
s settles the row at hand: it leaves AT WORK until it needs you again, and the

18
00:01:39.106 --> 00:01:41.334
heading counts what is settled.

19
00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.707
A row that needs you does not go.

20
00:01:43.707 --> 00:01:47.229
Colon unsettle, or the jump line, brings it back.

21
00:01:54.264 --> 00:01:56.711
Let the simulation run again.

22
00:01:56.711 --> 00:02:03.460
Your conversation with an agent is v from its row; here, the leader's reply to a

23
00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:04.135
request.

24
00:02:04.135 --> 00:02:11.137
Inside it, v chooses lines: j and k grow the choice, w and b go word by word, and y

25
00:02:11.137 --> 00:02:17.886
copies them as plain text, cleaned of anything that should not leave the screen.

26
00:02:17.886 --> 00:02:24.635
m marks a line to come back to with the apostrophe; marks are kept between runs.

27
00:02:34.805 --> 00:02:38.993
When a project's work is done, colon archive puts it away.

28
00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:44.914
For ten seconds, u still keeps it; then its agents go to sleep with their sessions

29
00:02:44.914 --> 00:02:49.896
and their mail, and a fresh project of the same name takes its place.

30
00:02:52.846 --> 00:02:56.744
Capital A lists the archives by checkout.

31
00:02:56.744 --> 00:03:04.253
Enter opens one as it was, read-only: its Home, its journal, what still waited.

32
00:03:04.253 --> 00:03:11.858
Escape comes back, and r restores it, asleep, while the fresh project gives way.

33
00:03:20.221 --> 00:03:24.232
And every key can be bound to one of your own, in a key file.

